text:
Maya: Heads-up — on mobile (iPhone SE / 360px) the runs table is getting vertically clipped when the left rail collapses into the condensed rail. Screenshot: https://redwood-internal.screens/example1.png. Repro: /runs -> narrow to 360px -> open a row action.

Jonah: Ack. Do you mean rows are literally cut off or are they hidden behind the bottom nav? :thinking_face:

Maya: Literal cutoff — see image, last ~6px of the row content truncated. Also the sidebar collapse animation causes a layout jump that makes rows reflow briefly.

Eli: I can repro on chrome mobile emulation. Suspect CSS using 100vh - header is the culprit (mobile browser UI changes). Using env(safe-area-inset-bottom) or listening for visualViewport resize helps.

Sam: Quick idea: move collapse breakpoint up to 420px and make the sidebar overlay instead of pushing content. Overlay avoids compressing table width and landing the actions under the sheet.

Aria: Accessibility nit — if we overlay the sidebar, we need a proper focus trap and aria-expanded on the toggle. Also ensure the row action menu is reachable via keyboard when overlay is open.

Jonah: +1 overlay, but overlay currently covers the action popover. Maybe action popovers should portal to body so they float above overlays. :+1:

Maya: here's a small CSS I tried locally — reduces the clip but doesn't solve the popover z-index (transform stacking context):
```css
@media (max-width: 420px) {
  .console-sidebar {
    position: fixed;
    left: 0;
    top: var(--header-height);
    bottom: 0;
    width: 240px;
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    transition: transform 200ms ease;
  }
  .console-sidebar.open { transform: translateX(0); }
  .table-wrap { padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom); }
}
```

Eli: That transform creates a new stacking context — any popover inside a transformed ancestor can be clipped under other layers. Best fix: render popover via portal/root-level layer and control its z-index relative to the overlay. Also ensure the popover uses position: fixed when portaled.

Sam: From an engineering standpoint: portal + focus trap + body-scroll-lock. For breakpoints, I tested 420 and 440 on a few devices; 440 gives fewer borderline squeezes on some android phones. We should pick a value after the design review.

Aria: Copy tweak suggestion: when the left rail changes behavior on narrow screens, use "Open menu" instead of "Collapse" for the button label (screen reader clarity). Also reduce tooltip delay on touch devices so it doesn't block taps.

Maya: Thanks — I'll prototype overlay + portal + aria tweaks and push a demo to the design sandbox. Can we decide the breakpoint by EOW? @Jonah @Eli :eyes: 

Jonah: I'll run visual diffs across the device matrix and test popover z-order. Aim for a PR by Thu.

design-bot: Pinned screenshot and test matrix to thread, added tag `mobile-responsive` and `a11y`.
